{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Natural World", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Visiting the Whales ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "extinct", "type": "name"}, {"content": "no longer existing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Organizations are trying to protect whales from becoming extinct.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about nature.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to convince ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause (someone) to believe firmly in the truth of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: One way of preserving whales has been to convince governments to do something.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "preservation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the action of keeping something or someone safe from harm ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All over the world, wildlife preservation organizations are trying to protect whales.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "porpoise ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small member of the whale family, related to the dolphin ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All the large whale species and many dolphins and porpoises can be seen regularly on tours that last from an hour to two weeks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to wipe out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to completely remove from existence ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If people kept hunting whales, they would wipe out some of the most fascinating mammals in the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to safeguard", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to protect ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If we could go back in time, we would be able to safeguard the world's whale population.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/>  Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/> What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I married Peter,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I would be happy.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" it snowed next July,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I would be very surprised.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I were you,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I would be jumping up and down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If we could go back in time, we would be able to safeguard the world's whale population.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "  If people kept hunting them, they would wipe out some of the most fascinating mammals in the world.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Giving Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals to give advice. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The most common modals for giving advice are:<br/><span class=\"italic\">should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. In this case, these modals add the meaning of advice. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should</span> is the most common modal used to give advice. <br/><span class=\"italic\">Ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">had better</span> are used for giving strong advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Verb\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" read\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" more about wildlife preservation.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" ought to \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" more careful about disposing of our garbage.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" had better \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" more to protect the whales.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<ul><li>In conversation, it is common to use contractions with <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>. </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We'd better do more to protect them. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Japanese public ought to be more aware of the need to preserve nature and especially to protect the whales. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and find a video featuring whales.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down your thoughts and impressions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your thoughts with a partner. Try to talk about solutions to the current problem of whale preservation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch a video about whales.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write notes about my thoughts and impressions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my thoughts with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "  I can talk about nature and the animal world.