All the large whale species and many dolphins and porpoises can be seen regularly on tours that last from an hour to two weeks.", "time": "28000"}, {"image": "", "id": 3, "text": "Japan is an example of this shift from whale hunting to whale watching. Until recently, Japan was a world leader in whale hunting. Today, the Japanese public ought to be more aware of the need to preserve nature and especially to protect the whales. Various organizations are working to make this happen. If we could go back in time, we would be able to safeguard the world's whale population.", "time": "47000"}], "video_src": "engenn7le12ob03re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "video", "title": ""}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}]}